Add a static-scale FP8 mode to the split-KV speculative verifier.

This patch is intentionally kernel-only. It is applied after
spec-decode-attn.patch and spec-decode-int8-kv.patch and does not yet hook the
FlashInfer backend. Keeping the kernel extension separate lets us validate FP8
math against a dequantized BF16 reference before changing runtime dispatch.

vLLM's normal per-layer FP8 KV cache stores E4M3 values plus one K and one V
scale for the layer. On SM80 the verifier loads the raw E4M3 cache, converts to
BF16 for tensor-core dot products, and folds the static scales into the same
places used by the existing per-token-head int8 path:

    score = (q . k_fp8_as_bf16) * k_scale
    value = (p * v_scale) . v_fp8_as_bf16

The per-token-head INT8 path remains unchanged. STATIC_QUANT and QUANT are
mutually exclusive.

Apply after patches/spec-decode-int8-kv.patch:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/spec-decode-fp8-kv-sm80.patch

Written against the repository's vLLM 0.27.1 patch stack.

--- a/v1/attention/ops/spec_decode_attn.py
+++ b/v1/attention/ops/spec_decode_attn.py
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ def _spec_attn_partial(
